          "title": "You'll want to know: متحمس",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "متحمس — mutaḥammis — \"excited, keen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ابني متحمس للرحلة إلى البحر. ibnī mutaḥammis li-r-riḥla ilā al-baḥr. My son is excited about the trip to the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes لـ for what you look forward to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "متحمس (mutaḥammis) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-m-s, \"to be hard, firm, vehement\" (Lane). Ḥamās, enthusiasm, which you know, is from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
